 that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","kind":"symbol","title":"Swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reproduces the runner reference’s fixed layer hierarchy and framing: a full-screen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"magenta canvas and a centered white card. The card maps "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":" Position to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its offset. Release projects momentum, applies the Drag patch’s logical bounds, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pulses Reset when both position axes are within the placed graph’s 100-point center"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tolerance."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Interaction_DragView","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview"}}}